From: PS5_Proton <local>
Subject: [PATCH] Game mode: flip a full-screen window's frames directly

A 2026-10-10 run (record removed from the tree; in git history) measured the same game in both routes: from
the launcher the broker flips its frames itself and no refresh is missed;
on the desktop each frame was copied into the scene and the desktop
composed (2.6 ms average), and a refresh was missed about once or twice a
second. Now, while a GPU window's frame is exactly what composing would
show (src/pw_window_direct.h: a complete snapshot, the client area the whole
screen, a screen-sized frame, no effects, clips covering the screen, nothing
visible above it), the frame goes to the display the way the launcher's
does: nothing is copied or composed, and the compositor thread looks at
nothing while the game keeps presenting. Other windows' frames update the
scene behind it without composing. A quiet game is looked at again every
100 ms; when game mode ends without a new frame, the window's image in the
scene is read back from the display's last flip, so composing never shows
a frame from before game mode. Entries and exits, and per client the frames
shown directly or composed and why, go to the record and to stderr.

Base: PS5_Vulkan 87a48676dda0977d5ba8ff1ddcf02816d41c443b + 0001-0005
